# --- Secrets / browser state -------------------------------------------------
# Local credentials for the PubMed/OpenAlex corroboration look-ups. tools/env.js
# reads this file at require time. It must never be committed: it holds a live
# API key, and a key in a query string would also be persisted into a report
# JSON by the failure notes, which is why crosscheck.js sends it as a header.
# .env.example is the tracked template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The persistent Playwright profile holds the signed-in Google session
# (cookies, tokens, cache). It must never be committed.
tools/.playwright-profile/

# The Playwright MCP server writes page snapshots, console logs and network
# traces into .playwright-mcp/ at the repo root as it works. They are debug
# scratch, not evidence, and a snapshot can contain a signed URL or session
# cookie from a paywalled host.
.playwright-mcp/

# --- Dependencies ------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/

# --- SQLite transient sidecars -----------------------------------------------
# The database itself (citation-catalog.sqlite) is tracked; these are the
# write-ahead log and shared-memory files that change while a process runs.
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-journal

# --- Recovery snapshots -------------------------------------------------------
# tools/build-catalog.js writes a verified VACUUM INTO snapshot here before any
# write, and never deletes one. They stay on disk as the local recovery path but
# are not committed: each is several MB and a new one appears on nearly every
# run, which would put tens of MB of near-identical binaries permanently into
# history. The tracked Database/citation-catalog.sqlite is the durable copy, and
# its own git history is the fallback (git log -- Database/citation-catalog.sqlite).
# Copy a snapshot somewhere tracked deliberately if one must survive long-term.
Database/Backups/

# --- Scratch runs and generated output ---------------------------------------
*.log
*.out.txt
tools/.tmp-*
tools/.pdf-fit-sample.*
tools/.pdf-header-sample.*

# --- Backup / superseded copies written by the re-print tools ---------------
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# --- Editor and OS noise -----------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.tmp

# --- Session scratch moved out of the repo root ------------------------------
# archived-scripts/ holds the one-off .cjs drivers and probes used during PDF
# retrieval; archived-logs/ holds their dumps, maps and notes. Kept on disk as
# the record of what was fetched and why, but they are ~150 MB of near-identical
# base64 captures and must not enter history. Nothing here is evidence.
# The `*` form (not `archived-scripts/`) is required to re-include the README:
# git cannot un-ignore a file inside a directory it has excluded wholesale.
archived-scripts/*
!archived-scripts/README.md
archived-logs/
